WEBVTT

00:00:11.345 --> 00:00:12.430
Get out of the way!

00:00:13.514 --> 00:00:15.016
[chuckles]

00:00:16.392 --> 00:00:18.561
Hey, guys. Watch this.

00:00:31.574 --> 00:00:32.867
Step on it!

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.160
[chuckling]

00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:35.870
Do you always drive like this?

00:00:35.953 --> 00:00:38.080
Only when it's
strictly necessary.

00:00:38.164 --> 00:00:40.541
And it's always necessary.

00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:43.002
[music continues]

00:00:50.218 --> 00:00:51.636
[screams]

00:01:04.607 --> 00:01:06.400
There! The bridge! That's our exit.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.528
I gotcha.

00:01:13.616 --> 00:01:15.034
Piranha, check our six.

00:01:15.117 --> 00:01:16.244
I got it.

00:01:22.166 --> 00:01:23.167
[Piranha] All clear, papo.

00:01:28.047 --> 00:01:29.340
It's the Bad Guys!

00:01:29.423 --> 00:01:32.301
[music continues]

00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:39.934
Whoa.

00:01:43.354 --> 00:01:44.480
[all laughing]

00:01:46.065 --> 00:01:47.149
Uh-oh.

00:01:49.944 --> 00:01:52.613
Wolf, you got a secret plan,
or are we just dead?

00:01:52.697 --> 00:01:53.906
I'll let you know in a minute.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:55.032
The ramp.

00:01:55.741 --> 00:01:56.867
Yes?

00:01:56.951 --> 00:01:58.452
Punch it. I have an idea.

00:01:58.536 --> 00:02:01.038
Okay, new kid. Let's see what you got.

00:02:05.668 --> 00:02:06.961
[praying indistinctly]

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:15.803
-Rookie...
-Bam!

00:02:22.768 --> 00:02:24.061
[music continues]

00:02:31.819 --> 00:02:33.946
Whoo! Yeah, baby!

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.740
Welcome to the crew, kid.

00:02:35.823 --> 00:02:37.074
Call me "Webs."

00:02:37.158 --> 00:02:39.035
Ooh, punchy. Okay, okay.

00:02:40.703 --> 00:02:43.164
I am never driving another car ever again!

00:02:43.247 --> 00:02:44.248
[music ends]

00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:52.381
Nice carbon footprint, jackass!

00:02:52.465 --> 00:02:53.466
Classy.

00:02:58.346 --> 00:03:00.598
Come on. Easy, now. Easy, easy.

00:03:00.681 --> 00:03:02.266
Come on, girl. You got this.

00:03:03.976 --> 00:03:05.186
[sighs]

00:03:06.103 --> 00:03:07.605
[car alarm blaring]

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:14.362
Oh, hey. Look who it is. Get over here.

00:03:14.445 --> 00:03:16.072
Where you been keeping yourselves?

00:03:16.155 --> 00:03:18.240
Me? [scoffs] Oh.

00:03:18.324 --> 00:03:20.826
Terrific. Fantastic.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:25.498
I mean, not everyone believes it,
but the Bad Guys went good.

00:03:25.581 --> 00:03:27.041
<i>I'll spare you the details,</i>

00:03:27.124 --> 00:03:30.086
<i>but in a nutshell,
we felt the "wag" of doing good.</i>

00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:31.337
Made a couple of new friends...

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.548
-[in unison] Diane?
-You're the Crimson Paw?

00:03:34.632 --> 00:03:36.801
We took down Marmalade, a real bad guy.

00:03:36.884 --> 00:03:38.511
The Crimson Paw!

00:03:38.594 --> 00:03:41.013
Me? No, no-- She's the Crimson Paw.

00:03:41.097 --> 00:03:43.057
[Wolf] And surprised everyone
by turning ourselves in.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.476
Yeah, we had a pretty good run
as bad guys,

00:03:45.559 --> 00:03:47.728
but sometimes you got to
give up the thing you know

00:03:47.812 --> 00:03:49.855
<i>in order to find something better.</i>

00:03:50.648 --> 00:03:52.650
So here we are, law-abiding citizens

00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:54.568
starting over with a clean slate.

00:03:54.652 --> 00:03:59.699
And we cannot wait for society
to welcome us with open arms.

00:04:02.952 --> 00:04:06.455
A-And now you wanna work, uh, a-at a bank?

00:04:06.539 --> 00:04:09.125
Why not? Some of my
best memories are at banks.

00:04:09.208 --> 00:04:10.459
[chuckling]

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.630
Uh, you robbed us three times.

00:04:16.048 --> 00:04:17.591
[whispers] That was this bank?

00:04:17.675 --> 00:04:21.679
It says here that you saved the city
from an evil guinea pig,

00:04:21.762 --> 00:04:24.140
but aren't you a notorious criminal?

00:04:24.849 --> 00:04:26.892
Yes! No. M-Maybe? [farts]

00:04:26.976 --> 00:04:28.394
Sorry. Sorry, nerves. [chuckles]

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.897
[stammers] I can also do
a great tuna impression.

00:04:32.565 --> 00:04:34.608
[chuckles] It's like you're
talking to a tuna, right?

00:04:34.692 --> 00:04:37.695
Well, I'm proficient in
UNIX, Linux, Windows, Mac,

00:04:37.778 --> 00:04:40.156
and fluent in 87 coding languages,

00:04:40.239 --> 00:04:41.866
So yeah, I'm qualified.

00:04:41.949 --> 00:04:44.493
I see. And, um,
how do you explain this gap

00:04:44.577 --> 00:04:45.870
in your employment history?

00:04:46.579 --> 00:04:47.580
Uh...

00:04:47.663 --> 00:04:49.290
My salary expectations?

00:04:49.373 --> 00:04:51.292
Wow. That's a good question.

00:04:51.375 --> 00:04:53.419
No one's ever given me money
on purpose before.

00:04:53.502 --> 00:04:55.004
Great at Secret Santa?

00:04:55.087 --> 00:04:56.422
Yeah, how does that--

00:04:56.505 --> 00:04:57.923
W-Wait. Don't tell me.

00:04:58.591 --> 00:05:00.968
Bath bomb. Lavender.

00:05:02.386 --> 00:05:04.430
And how would you react
if you saw a coworker

00:05:04.513 --> 00:05:07.475
doing something that
violates company policy?

00:05:08.058 --> 00:05:10.311
Snitches get stitches
and sleep with the fishes.

00:05:10.394 --> 00:05:12.730
You know what? Can I get
another chance at that one?

00:05:14.064 --> 00:05:15.941
I think we got everything we need.

00:05:16.025 --> 00:05:17.359
So great to meet you.

00:05:17.443 --> 00:05:18.736
Thanks for coming in.

00:05:18.819 --> 00:05:21.071
Uh, we're gonna... We're gonna pass.

00:05:22.323 --> 00:05:27.995
Look, Craig. Anyone who wants to change
needs to start somewhere, right?

00:05:28.078 --> 00:05:30.664
So, I'm just asking for a chance.

00:05:31.248 --> 00:05:32.583
Just a chance.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.293
Please?

00:05:36.587 --> 00:05:38.130
You know what, Mr. Wolf?

00:05:38.214 --> 00:05:40.800
[stammers] I might have
something here for you.

00:05:40.883 --> 00:05:41.967
I'm gonna give you a call.

00:05:42.551 --> 00:05:43.886
[stammers] Gee, really?

00:05:43.969 --> 00:05:45.763
Craig, that's great!

00:05:45.846 --> 00:05:48.307
-Number is on my résumé there.
-Okay.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:51.602
-And this has been just great.
-Uh, you can let go now.

00:05:51.685 --> 00:05:53.020
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to--

00:05:53.103 --> 00:05:56.065
I got a job! This is fantastic, man.

00:05:57.525 --> 00:05:59.026
Oh, by the way, Craig, you know...

00:06:03.155 --> 00:06:04.448
Ah.

00:06:04.532 --> 00:06:06.033
Yeah. Got it.

00:06:10.788 --> 00:06:11.956
[sighs]

